France recorded a rise of nearly 30 percent in deaths during the week beginning 22 June, the peak of the country's record-breaking heatwave, the public health authority said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/da0f433e-76a8-11f1-8e89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T220613Z-1012512868-RC2A5MADKJ7Y-RTRMADP-3-USA-WEATHER-HEAT-NEW-YORK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/da0f433e-76a8-11f1-8e89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T220613Z-1012512868-RC2A5MADKJ7Y-RTRMADP-3-USA-WEATHER-HEAT-NEW-YORK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">076ddfd0-76ad-11f1-aedd-518d93cbeb2e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 07:06:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/da0f433e-76a8-11f1-8e89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T220613Z-1012512868-RC2A5MADKJ7Y-RTRMADP-3-USA-WEATHER-HEAT-NEW-YORK.jpg">© Jordan Tovin/ Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France issues water safety alert after more than 90 drowning deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-france-issues-water-safety-alert-after-more-than-90-drowning-deaths-heatwave</link><description>
The French government said more than 90 people have died by drowning since 19 June, as authorities and swimming bodies stepped up warnings during a summer marked by intense heat and more people seeking relief in rivers, lakes, canals and pools.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28f3ca9e-7611-11f1-9b77-55a00649bc60</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 15:03:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg">AFP - ARNAUD FINISTRE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on France</category><title>Podcast: Adapting to heat, France's fitness boom, Paris Mosque at 100</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-france/20260702-podcast-climate-adaptation-heatwave-fitness-paris-mosque-algeria-france</link><description>
As France's record-breaking heatwave last week raises questions about how the country will have to adapt to a warming climate, we look at what that could mean for French culture. We also explore the country's growing interest in fitness – driven in part by its most popular YouTuber – and examine how the Grand Mosque of Paris, which marks its centenary this year, became both a symbol of Islam in France and a recurring source of political tension.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34686256-760a-11f1-bf8b-a7557f473b29</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 14:30:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sarah Elzas</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfires spread across southern France, as heatwave reignites forest concerns</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-wildfires-spread-across-southern-france-as-heatwave-reignites-forest-concerns</link><description>
Wildfires have broken out across southern France, forcing evacuations and stretching firefighting teams as the country prepares for the third heatwave of the summer, with the country's forests under increasing threat from climate change and disputes over logging.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76a15890-75f0-11f1-ae1f-a949136140ad</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 13:36:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg">AFP - LIONEL BONAVENTURE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris death penalty congress warns abolition cannot be taken for granted</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-macron-warns-death-penalty-debate-is-back-as-executions-rise-worldwide</link><description>
The fight to abolish the death penalty remains "eminently contemporary", French President Emmanuel Macron said as campaigners, judges and former death row prisoners gathered in Paris this week for the World Congress Against the Death Penalty, amid rising executions worldwide and renewed support for capital punishment in some democracies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f30e478e-7524-11f1-b65e-7129b96364f7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 09:44:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg">ASSOCIATED PRESS - Pat Sullivan</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France advances assisted dying law with strict rules and safeguards</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-france-advances-assisted-dying-law-with-safeguards-and-strict-rules</link><description>
France's National Assembly has approved a new version of a bill creating a legal right to assisted dying, bringing the country closer to a major change in end-of-life care. The legislation sets out who could qualify, how requests would be made and the safeguards designed to prevent abuse of the law. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">859a835a-7558-11f1-8d03-c36d4528ccb7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 06:05:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg">AP - Mosa'ab Elshamy</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France confirms dates for 2027 presidential election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260701-france-confirms-dates-for-2027-presidential-election-april-may</link><description>
France will hold the first round of its next presidential election on 18 April 2027 and the runoff on 2 May after the government formally approved the dates at Wednesday's cabinet meeting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0669c7d6-754d-11f1-af71-d16dd1da17f0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 14:41:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg">© THEO ROUBY / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French justice system to re-examine 88,000 child abuse claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260630-french-justice-system-to-re-examine-88-000-child-abuse-claims</link><description>
Some 88,000 complaints regarding sexual violence against children are being re-examined by investigative services – a figure higher than the 70,000 initially ordered by Justice Minister Gérald Darmanin last month. This comes in the wake of the murder of 11-year-old Lyhanna, whose death prompted public outrage over the state's mishandling of child abuse cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2db850c4-6377-11f1-b7e4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6CM8GC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2db850c4-6377-11f1-b7e4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6CM8GC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82c0a524-7463-11f1-b96b-8da6f2af1ad5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 10:02:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2db850c4-6377-11f1-b7e4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6CM8GC.jpg">© Behrouz Mehri / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Volvic to appeal after French court rules green claims were misleading</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260630-volvic-to-appeal-after-french-court-rules-green-claims-were-misleading</link><description>
The bottled water brand Volvic has been found guilty of “misleading commercial practices” by the Paris Commercial Court over environmental claims made on its mineral water bottles, including that they were “carbon neutral” or “100 percent recyclable”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/72b36e5e-73b0-11f1-ae7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3455573.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/72b36e5e-73b0-11f1-ae7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3455573.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3142793e-7391-11f1-a80c-7d8eb55a1ec6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 05:57:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/72b36e5e-73b0-11f1-ae7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3455573.jpg">AFP - THOMAS COEX</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Anti-independence parties make gains in New Caledonia provincial poll</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260629-anti-independence-parties-make-gains-in-new-caledonia-provincial-poll</link><description>
New Caledonia’s non-independence parties gained ground in provincial elections on Sunday, according to provisional results, in a vote expected to shape the next round of talks with France over the Pacific territory’s future status.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/70110d5c-73b8-11f1-bc34-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8K42CT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/70110d5c-73b8-11f1-bc34-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8K42CT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">683813b8-7391-11f1-ac7d-7d8eb55a1ec6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 15:40:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/70110d5c-73b8-11f1-bc34-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8K42CT.jpg">AFP - DELPHINE MAYEUR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France opens investigation after 11 killed in skydiving plane crash near Nancy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260629-france-opens-investigation-after-11-killed-in-skydiving-plane-crash-near-nancy</link><description>
French investigators have begun examining the cause of a small aircraft crash near Nancy that killed 11 people, including private nurses making their first skydiving jump, in what officials say is the deadliest light aircraft accident recorded in France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/73d8fcfe-730b-11f1-a8d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/images-205.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/73d8fcfe-730b-11f1-a8d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/images-205.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">98fe7238-7384-11f1-a16b-11a28589ba96</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 07:11:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/73d8fcfe-730b-11f1-a8d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/images-205.jpg">© Jean-Christophe Verhaegen/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron hosts Oman sultan for talks on toll-free reopening of Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260629-macron-hosts-oman-sultan-for-talks-on-toll-free-reopening-of-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron hosts Oman's Sultan Haitham bin Tariq on Monday for the Gulf leader's first official visit to France, with talks expected to focus on securing the toll-free reopening of the Strait of Hormuz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1b3a5e6c-4188-11f1-a977-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26116354137889.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1b3a5e6c-4188-11f1-a977-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26116354137889.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56b40ab4-7145-11f1-b5cd-b38f59619540</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 06:04:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1b3a5e6c-4188-11f1-a977-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26116354137889.jpg">AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's deadly heatwave triggers accusations of government inaction</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260628-french-government-under-fire-as-hospitals-face-excess-heatwave-deaths</link><description>
After 11 days of an exceptional heatwave and in the face of the heavy human toll that is beginning to emerge, politicians are accusing the French government of "incompetence" and "inaction." This comes after health officials said Sunday there had been around 1,000 more deaths than expected compared to previous months.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/66a286ea-72ca-11f1-b9e3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B82X2WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/66a286ea-72ca-11f1-b9e3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B82X2WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee325518-72de-11f1-a859-494a63b910f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 14:16:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/66a286ea-72ca-11f1-b9e3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B82X2WE.jpg">AFP - PHILIPPE LOPEZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Remains of people exhibited in ‘human zoos’ to be returned to French Guiana</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260628-remains-of-people-exhibited-in-human-zoos-to-be-returned-to-french-guiana</link><description>
In 1892, around 30 men, women and children from the Kali’na and Arawak peoples of French Guiana were brought to Paris to be put on display at "human zoos". Six of them did not survive the winter. A bill allowing the repatriation of their remains to their homeland has now received final approval – the culmination of a long struggle waged by their descendants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/064212e0-6828-11f1-99d8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Chamane.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/064212e0-6828-11f1-99d8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Chamane.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb6bf5d8-6e35-11f1-8f95-7ba779e4a441</guid><pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 12:24:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/064212e0-6828-11f1-99d8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Chamane.jpeg">© Arame Mbengue / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>New Caledonia election tests territory's future after unrest and deadlock</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260628-new-caledonia-election-tests-territory-s-future-after-unrest-and-deadlock</link><description>
Polling stations have just closed in New Caledonia following provincial elections in a vote that will test the French Pacific territory's future after years of political deadlock and unrest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/17b9fc4e-72c4-11f1-ae9c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/People-voting-in-New-Caledonia-28-June-2026-AFP-Delphine-Mayeur.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/17b9fc4e-72c4-11f1-ae9c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/People-voting-in-New-Caledonia-28-June-2026-AFP-Delphine-Mayeur.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c887e44-6fb3-11f1-bfde-895fd0b87d64</guid><pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 07:26:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/17b9fc4e-72c4-11f1-ae9c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/People-voting-in-New-Caledonia-28-June-2026-AFP-Delphine-Mayeur.jpg">AFP - DELPHINE MAYEUR</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>British historian defends artistic licence in controversial de Gaulle biopic</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260627-british-historian-defends-artistic-licence-in-controversial-de-gaulle-biopic</link><description>
The big-budget biopic La Bataille de Gaulle, which premiered at Cannes in May, has drawn the ire of French historians for liberties it takes with historical record. But Julian Jackson, the British scholar whose biography inspired the film, says some things are more important than the details. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b5aedc5c-5f38-11f1-885f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/La-Bataille-de-Gaulle-Simon-Abkarian-Cannes-2026-Credit-Malgosia-Abramowska.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b5aedc5c-5f38-11f1-885f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/La-Bataille-de-Gaulle-Simon-Abkarian-Cannes-2026-Credit-Malgosia-Abramowska.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1bd63252-7166-11f1-8fad-c19e380bf25d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:12:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b5aedc5c-5f38-11f1-885f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/La-Bataille-de-Gaulle-Simon-Abkarian-Cannes-2026-Credit-Malgosia-Abramowska.jpg">© Malgosia Abramowska</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Punishing heatwave exposes cracks in France's nuclear power fleet</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260626-punishing-heatwave-exposes-cracks-in-france-s-nuclear-power-fleet-reactor</link><description>
Three French nuclear plants halted production during this week's record-breaking heatwave as rivers became too warm to cool them, raising questions over the long-term future of Europe's biggest nuclear fleet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5f2d494c-10b9-11ea-819d-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-18t000000z_1975114624_rc19d5eae900_rtrmadp_3_edf-nuclearpower_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5f2d494c-10b9-11ea-819d-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-18t000000z_1975114624_rc19d5eae900_rtrmadp_3_edf-nuclearpower_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6176a34-707c-11f1-a529-c7d93de76560</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 16:00:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5f2d494c-10b9-11ea-819d-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-18t000000z_1975114624_rc19d5eae900_rtrmadp_3_edf-nuclearpower_0.jpg">REUTERS/Benoit Tessier</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Historic heatwave catches Europe's fashion industry unprepared</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260626-historic-heat-wave-catches-europe-s-fashion-industry-unprepared</link><description>
The most coveted accessory at the Paris Fashion Week shows this week was not a bag, a sneaker or a watch. It was an ice pack.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3146c48-7152-11f1-ac57-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26174738668640.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3146c48-7152-11f1-ac57-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26174738668640.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27eba1c6-7166-11f1-8c8e-7f9657189cb1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 13:55:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3146c48-7152-11f1-ac57-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26174738668640.jpg">AP Photo/Aurelien Morissard - Aurelien Morissard</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France heatwave overwhelms hospitals and forces Pride march delay</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260626-france-heatwave-overwhelms-hospitals-and-forces-pride-march-delay</link><description>
Emergency doctors at one of Paris's biggest hospitals warned on Friday that wards had become dangerously overcrowded after a week of soaring temperatures, as authorities restricted public alcohol consumption, organisers postponed the annual Pride march and €130 million was pledged to help schools adapt to climate change.
